WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.733
Hebrews, Chapter Eight.

2
00:00:01.733 --> 00:00:19.067
Now of the things which we have spoken this is the sum: We have such an high priest, who is set on the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in the heavens; A minister of the sanctuary, and of the true tabernacle, which the Lord pitched, and not man.

3
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:27.333
For every high priest is ordained to offer gifts and sacrifices: wherefore it is of necessity that this man have somewhat also to offer.

4
00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:42.000
For if he were on earth, he should not be a priest, seeing that there are priests that offer gifts according to the law: Who serve unto the example and shadow of heavenly things, as Moses was admonished of God when he was about to make the tabernacle: for, See, saith he,

5
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.000
that thou make all things according to the pattern shewed to thee in the mount.

6
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:55.067
But now hath he obtained a more excellent ministry, by how much also he is the mediator of a better covenant, which was established upon better promises.

7
00:00:55.067 --> 00:01:00.933
For if that first covenant had been faultless, then should no place have been sought for the second.

8
00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:10.000
For finding fault with them, he saith, Behold, the days come, saith the Lord, when I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah:

9
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.667
Not according to the covenant that I made with their fathers in the day when I took them by the hand to lead them out of the land of Egypt; because they continued not in my covenant, and I regarded them not, saith the Lord.

10
00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:35.733
For this is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel after those days, saith the Lord; I will put my laws into their mind, and write them in their hearts: and I will be to them a God, and they shall be to me a people: And they shall not teach every man his neighbour,

11
00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:42.133
and every man his brother, saying, Know the Lord: for all shall know me, from the least to the greatest.

12
00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:48.400
For I will be merciful to their unrighteousness, and their sins and their iniquities will I remember no more.

13
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.000
In that he saith, A new covenant, he hath made the first old.

14
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.400
Now that which decayeth and waxeth old is ready to vanish away.

